{ stop_wait in Kontakt 8.13.1, by when the note plays (measured 2026-10-28).
  Render a held note (1.5 s) through ANALOG STRINGS with this as an
  appended slot-1 script (scratch librender2.py APPEND_KSP, APPEND_SLOT=1).
  Timing only: slot 1 runs before ANALOG's main script, which is fine here.
    one wait(10 s),  stop_wait(.., 0): note at the release
    two wait(10 s),  stop_wait(.., 0): note at 12.9 s (release + 10 s)
    two wait(10 s),  stop_wait(.., 1): note at the release
  So 0 ends only the current wait; 1 also lets every later wait pass.
  Pinned by kontra-host tests/script.rs stop_wait_ends_the_current_wait_or_every_wait. }
on init
  declare $id
end on
on note
  ignore_event($EVENT_ID)
  $id := $NI_CALLBACK_ID
  wait(10000000)
  wait(10000000)
  play_note(72, 100, 0, 1000000)
end on
on release
  stop_wait($id, 0)
end on
